---
description: Comment policy - keep only comments that explain non-obvious "why"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code comments

Default to no comment. Add one only when the code can't explain itself:

- A non-obvious workaround or gotcha (a library quirk, a race-condition fix)
- A deliberate decision that looks wrong at first glance (e.g. "no authGuard
  here on purpose")
- A contract/invariant that's easy to violate by accident

Don't write a comment that just restates the line below it, explains basic
language/framework mechanics, or narrates what's about to happen. Delete a
comment like that instead of keeping it "for documentation."

```ts
// ❌ restates the code
// Set loading to true
this.loading.set(true);

// ✅ explains non-obvious "why"
// Signals, not plain fields: writeValue() is called externally by the Forms
// module, and under OnPush a plain field mutated from outside never
// triggers a re-render.
protected readonly value = signal('');
```
